1. Check Docker version

docker --version


2. Test Docker installation

docker run hello-world


3. Go to Desktop

cd Desktop


4. Create project folder

mkdir docker-python-app


5. Enter project folder

cd docker-python-app


6. Check project files

dir


7. Build Docker image

docker build -t my-python-app .


8. Check Docker images

docker images


9. Run Docker container

docker run -d -p 5000:5000 --name my-python-container my-python-app


10. Check running containers

docker ps


11. Open the application

http://localhost:5000


12. View container logs

docker logs my-python-container


13. Stop the container

docker stop my-python-container


14. Start the container again

docker start my-python-container


15. Check running containers

docker ps


16. Remove the container

docker rm my-python-container


17. Check all containers

docker ps -a


18. Check Docker images

docker images
